<title>AUSTRALIA: Helix places 4.2 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Helix places 4.2 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold explorer Helix Resources NL said on Thursday it had placed 4.2 million shares to long term investors through J.B. Were &amp; Son at A$3.25 a share for further exploration in the Gawler Craton region of South Australia.</p>
<p>Helix's shares were unchanged at A$3.70 at 10.30 a.m. (2330 GMT), up from 45 cents on Monday last week before it announced promising drilling results from the Gawler Craton region.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
